
                                VARIABLES
                                =========

As with most old fashioned line BASICs there are only 2 main types
of variable: numeric and string. Numeric can take any floating point number
and have a name such as "abc" whilst strings can take any string value and
have any name except there must be a dollar sign on the end. Numeric and
string variables with the same name except for the dollar sign are allowed.

eg: a = 3
    a$ = "hello"

Arrays are permitted up to a maximum of 6 dimensions.

eg:
   10 DATA "hello","cruel","world"
   20 RESTORE 10
   30 DIM a(10),b$(3)
   40 FOR f=1 TO 10: a(f)=f*2: NEXT
   50 FOR f=1 TO 3: READ b$(f): NEXT
 
   10 DIM screen(screen_width,screen_height)
   20 FOR y=1 TO screen_height
   30     FOR x=1 TO screen_width
   40         screen(x,y)=0
   50     NEXT
   60 NEXT

